A||||4||Brian84SE||84/85 camshaft-what's the difference?||||1||
Z||000000||Brian84SE||09-09-2000||06:58 PM||||I am still trying to tell what the difference is between the 84 (flat lifter) and 85 (roller lifter) camshaft (4 cyl). The reason is the rebuilt block I got casting# says it's an 85.  So I need to know whether to get roller lifters or not. Comparing the cam quickly (without removing the cam) with my 84 block, shows only about a .030 difference in lobe height.  How different should a roller cam look? ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Rodrv6||09-09-2000||10:16 PM||||I'm not sure if you can really tell the difference just by looking.  The lobe profile will be nearly the same on both types.  The biggest difference is probably the way the lobes are ground.  Flat lifter cams usually have a small amount of taper on the lobe so that the lifter will rotate in its bore every time the valve is opened.  You probably couldn't tell without taking the cam out and making some careful measurements with a micrometer.  Also, if you are going to use roller lifters you will need the guide plates and locater springs to hold them in proper alignment and not spin in their bores.<P>------------------<BR>Rod Schneider, Woodstock, Ga.  84 SE||||reg||1
Z||000002||Will||09-09-2000||11:10 PM||||I don't know the specifics of the block design, but if it calls for roller lifters, you should use roller lifters. You should be able to tell by inspection of the block along side a roller lifter and a flat lifter.<BR>     The kicker is that a roller cam is made through a different process than a flat lifter cam. Using a roller cam with flat lifters or roller lifters with a flat cam will result in premature wear of one or both components.||||reg||1
Z||000003||theogre||09-09-2000||11:33 PM||||It's not the block that's the issue. It's the cam.<P>As I said in the other thread,,,,, If whoever you got this from can't or won't tell you whats in it the you need to start from scratch. You will have to buy a cam and lifter set Or get a known good used set. Putting new lifters on a used cam is a failure waiting to happen.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Brian84SE||09-10-2000||08:51 PM||||O.K.  I pulled both cams and compared them side by side.  Dimensionally, they were close.  It was the profile of the lobe that was a little different.||||reg||1
